CHAPTER.VERS:
And Moses spoke to the people, saying, Arm

          {+}
         men from among you

          {+}
         for the war, that they may go against Midian, to execute Yahweh's vengeance on Midian.

Of every tribe a thousand, throughout all the tribes of Israel, you

          {+}
         will send to the war.

And Moses said to them, Have you

          {+}
         saved all the women alive?

And encamp

          {+}
         outside the camp seven days: whoever has killed any person, and whoever has touched any slain, purify yourselves on the third day and on the seventh day, you

          {+}
         and your

          {+}
         captives.

And as to every garment, and all that is made of skin, and all work of goats' [hair], and all things made of wood, you

          {+}
         will purify yourselves.

everything that may go into fire, you

          {+}
         will make to go through the fire, and it will be clean; nevertheless it will be purified with the water for impurity: and all that does not go into fire you

          {+}
         will make to go through the water.

And you

          {+}
         will wash your

          {+}
         clothes on the seventh day, and you

          {+}
         will be clean; and afterward you

          {+}
         will come into the camp.
